Subject: [PATCH] test(browse): pin the busy-is-not-dead decision table; move
 decideDaemonRestart to a side-effect-free module

decideDaemonRestart was documented as pure and exported for unit coverage and had no test.
The first attempt to test it could not import cli.ts on Windows (the module throws at load
when the server bundle is absent), so the decision and its budget constant move to
browse/src/daemon-restart-decision.ts and cli.ts re-exports them. Six cases pin the IRON
RULE: an alive pid is never auto-killed; only --force-restart on an unresponsive daemon does.

Written by an ai-registry intake run (intake-gstack-0902) as a task row against the source
tree; not a PR.
